{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MMuwisxGypZoWQbDJFNHs8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"task_id\": \"e6-t09\",\n3\t  \"unresolved_distinctions\": [\n4\t    {\n5\t      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n6\t      \"question\": \"What is the minimum vertex cover size k for the graph in package/artifacts/graph.json?\",\n7\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"The package supplies only the raw graph (7 vertices, 9 edges); no cover size has been derived or recorded anywhere in the evidence state.\",\n8\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A derivation establishing k: a cover of size k exhibited together with a demonstration (e.g. exhaustive search over subsets, or a lower-bound argument) that no cover of size k-1 exists.\",\n9\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n10\t        \"Must be derived from package/artifacts/graph.json as given, covering all nine listed edges.\",\n11\t        \"The method used must be stated, per the deliverable's 'method' field and E-A's 'with its method stated' condition.\"\n12\t      ],\n13\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n14\t        \"E-A\"\n15\t      ],\n16\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n17\t      \"features\": {\n18\t        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n19\t        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n20\t        \"contamination\": false,\n21\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n22\t        \"spans_sessions\": false\n23\t      }\n24\t    },\n25\t    {\n26\t      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n27\t      \"question\": \"What is the complete first enumeration (E-A) of ALL vertex covers of minimum size k, each reported as a sorted vertex list, with the enumeration method stated?\",\n28\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"No enumeration exists yet; completeness is the deliverable, and the raw graph alone does not settle which size-k subsets are covers or whether a candidate list has missed one.\",\n29\t      \"required_evidence\": \"One complete candidate enumeration of the minimum-size covers (an exhaustive procedure over the search space, e.g. checking all vertex subsets of size k) with the method recorded alongside the list.\",\n30\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n31\t        \"E-A: 'one complete candidate enumeration with its method stated' \\u2014 the enumeration must be complete over the whole space and its production method must be reported.\",\n32\t        \"Each cover must be reported as its sorted vertex list, and the item list itself sorted, per the deliverable shape.\"\n33\t      ],\n34\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n35\t        \"E-A\"\n36\t      ],\n37\t      \"dependencies\": [\n38\t        \"Q1\"\n39\t      ],\n40\t      \"features\": {\n41\t        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n42\t        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n43\t        \"contamination\": false,\n44\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n45\t        \"spans_sessions\": false\n46\t      }\n47\t    },\n48\t    {\n49\t      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n50\t      \"question\": \"What does a second complete enumeration of the same space yield when produced without access to the first enumeration or any of its intermediate work (E-B)?\",\n51\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"No causally separated enumeration exists. The worker process that produces E-A cannot supply it: any enumeration it performs after (or while) forming the first one has access to the first enumeration by construction, which E-B's authorship/access condition explicitly forbids.\",\n52\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A complete enumeration of the minimum-size vertex covers produced by a process whose inputs include the graph but exclude the first enumeration, its intermediate work, and the worker's conclusions \\u2014 i.e. a separately launched, causally isolated process seeded only with package/artifacts/graph.json and the task statement.\",\n53\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n54\t        \"E-B: 'produced without access to the first enumeration or any of its intermediate work' \\u2014 the producing process must be causally separated from the E-A author's reasoning and outputs.\",\n55\t        \"The isolated process may (and must) see the raw graph; the exclusion applies to the first enumeration and its intermediate work, not to the package artifact itself.\",\n56\t        \"The second enumeration must cover the same space (all minimum-size covers) to be usable for E-C's mutual-support condition.\"\n57\t      ],\n58\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n59\t        \"E-B\"\n60\t      ],\n61\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n62\t      \"features\": {\n63\t        \"locally_resolvable\": false,\n64\t        \"requires_isolation\": true,\n65\t        \"contamination\": true,\n66\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": true,\n67\t        \"spans_sessions\": true\n68\t      }\n69\t    },\n70\t    {\n71\t      \"id\": \"Q4\",\n72\t      \"question\": \"What is the final merged answer (E-C): the union of both enumerations, with any item found by only one enumeration flagged, and is the completeness claim admissible?\",\n73\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"The merge cannot exist before both enumerations exist, and the completeness claim is admissible only when supported by both; with zero or one enumeration in hand the claim is unsupported and 'complete' can at best be PENDING-INTEGRATION.\",\n74\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A deterministic merge of the E-A and E-B enumerations: the union as sorted lists, per-item flags for anything found by only one side, and a completeness verdict set true only if both independent enumerations support it.\",\n75\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n76\t        \"E-C: 'the completeness claim is admissible only when supported by both enumerations' \\u2014 the claim inherits E-B's admissibility; if the second enumeration is not causally independent, the completeness claim fails regardless of correctness.\",\n77\t        \"Any item found by only one enumeration must be flagged in the merged answer.\",\n78\t        \"Deliverable shape: result.json with items (all covers, sorted), method, and complete as boolean or PENDING-INTEGRATION.\"\n79\t      ],\n80\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n81\t        \"E-C\"\n82\t      ],\n83\t      \"dependencies\": [\n84\t        \"Q2\",\n85\t        \"Q3\"\n86\t      ],\n87\t      \"features\": {\n88\t        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n89\t        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n90\t        \"contamination\": false,\n91\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n92\t        \"spans_sessions\": false\n93\t      }\n94\t    }\n95\t  ]\n96\t}\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10d2f9d5-39ad-4be7-ba55-d60a25ae2cff","uuid":"90cd0d46-50b8-4c3a-8790-ab4aa805d185","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:40:02.868Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t09/shadow/exec-ws/distinctions.json","content":"{\n  \"task_id\": \"e6-t09\",\n  \"unresolved_distinctions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n      \"question\": \"What is the minimum vertex cover size k for the graph in package/artifacts/graph.json?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"The package supplies only the raw graph (7 vertices, 9 edges); no cover size has been derived or recorded anywhere in the evidence state.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A derivation establishing k: a cover of size k exhibited together with a demonstration (e.g. exhaustive search over subsets, or a lower-bound argument) that no cover of size k-1 exists.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"Must be derived from package/artifacts/graph.json as given, covering all nine listed edges.\",\n        \"The method used must be stated, per the deliverable's 'method' field and E-A's 'with its method stated' condition.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n        \"E-A\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n      \"question\": \"What is the complete first enumeration (E-A) of ALL vertex covers of minimum size k, each reported as a sorted vertex list, with the enumeration method stated?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"No enumeration exists yet; completeness is the deliverable, and the raw graph alone does not settle which size-k subsets are covers or whether a candidate list has missed one.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"One complete candidate enumeration of the minimum-size covers (an exhaustive procedure over the search space, e.g. checking all vertex subsets of size k) with the method recorded alongside the list.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"E-A: 'one complete candidate enumeration with its method stated' \\u2014 the enumeration must be complete over the whole space and its production method must be reported.\",\n        \"Each cover must be reported as its sorted vertex list, and the item list itself sorted, per the deliverable shape.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n        \"E-A\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"Q1\"\n      ],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"question\": \"What does a second complete enumeration of the same space yield when produced without access to the first enumeration or any of its intermediate work (E-B)?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"No causally separated enumeration exists. The worker process that produces E-A cannot supply it: any enumeration it performs after (or while) forming the first one has access to the first enumeration by construction, which E-B's authorship/access condition explicitly forbids.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A complete enumeration of the minimum-size vertex covers produced by a process whose inputs include the graph but exclude the first enumeration, its intermediate work, and the worker's conclusions \\u2014 i.e. a separately launched, causally isolated process seeded only with package/artifacts/graph.json and the task statement.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"E-B: 'produced without access to the first enumeration or any of its intermediate work' \\u2014 the producing process must be causally separated from the E-A author's reasoning and outputs.\",\n        \"The isolated process may (and must) see the raw graph; the exclusion applies to the first enumeration and its intermediate work, not to the package artifact itself.\",\n        \"The second enumeration must cover the same space (all minimum-size covers) to be usable for E-C's mutual-support condition.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n        \"E-B\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": false,\n        \"requires_isolation\": true,\n        \"contamination\": true,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": true,\n        \"spans_sessions\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q4\",\n      \"question\": \"What is the final merged answer (E-C): the union of both enumerations, with any item found by only one enumeration flagged, and is the completeness claim admissible?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"The merge cannot exist before both enumerations exist, and the completeness claim is admissible only when supported by both; with zero or one enumeration in hand the claim is unsupported and 'complete' can at best be PENDING-INTEGRATION.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A deterministic merge of the E-A and E-B enumerations: the union as sorted lists, per-item flags for anything found by only one side, and a completeness verdict set true only if both independent enumerations support it.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"E-C: 'the completeness claim is admissible only when supported by both enumerations' \\u2014 the claim inherits E-B's admissibility; if the second enumeration is not causally independent, the completeness claim fails regardless of correctness.\",\n        \"Any item found by only one enumeration must be flagged in the merged answer.\",\n        \"Deliverable shape: result.json with items (all covers, sorted), method, and complete as boolean or PENDING-INTEGRATION.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n        \"E-C\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"Q2\",\n        \"Q3\"\n      ],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","numLines":97,"startLine":1,"totalLines":97}}}
